+# Audit 0.20.0: the printable report
+
+Method: graphic-design-fundamentals §13 (editorial / print sections: one page, hierarchy, real
+size) and impeccable (persuade-free, read mode), on `report_page_light`.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals §13
+
+| # | Check | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | One page a paediatrician can read in a minute. ✅ |
+| 2 | Concept | The summary first, the two weeks below. ✅ |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Title 22, captions 11 semibold muted, rows 11, bars. ✅ |
+| 4 | Contrast | Light theme ink on white; muted ≥ 4.5:1. ✅ |
+| 5 | Alignment | One left margin (48pt); values right-aligned to the same edge. ✅ |
+| 6 | Spacing | Even rows with hairlines; sections separated by space. ✅ |
+| 7 | Typography | Libre Franklin regular / semibold / bold; tabular-looking numbers on the right edge. ✅ |
+| 8 | Colour | Data colours only on the bars and legend, each beside a word. ✅ |
+| 9 | Consistency | Same words and numbers as Patterns. ✅ |
+| 10 | Simplicity | One page; nothing decorative. ✅ |
+| 11 | Real size | A4 at 595 × 842 pt; text ≥ 8pt. ✅ |
+| 12 | Accessibility | Legend words beside every colour; colour never alone. ✅ |
+| 13 | Production | Vector text and shapes in a real PDF; no raster. ✅ |
+
+Fixed in this release: the first page said "Today" and "Yesterday", which is wrong on paper read
+later; every date is absolute now (`Format.dayAbsolute`).
+
+## impeccable critique (read mode)
+
+| # | Heuristic | Score | Note |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | System status | 4 | "Exported" after saving. |
+| 2 | Real world | 4 | "Report for the doctor". |
+| 3 | Control | 4 | The parent chooses where it goes. |
+| 4 | Consistency | 4 | Same figures as Patterns. |
+| 5 | Error prevention | 3 | Empty sections are left out. |
+| 6 | Recognition | 4 | Legend and labels on the page. |
+| 7 | Efficiency | 4 | Two taps from Settings. |
+| 8 | Aesthetic | 4 | Quiet, typographic. |
+| 9 | Error recovery | 3 | A failure says so. |
+| 10 | Help | 4 | The footer says what it is and is not. |
+| | **Total** | **38/40** | |
